+## ms-parse-compound
+
+The API provides exported parseCompound(str: string): number for human duration sums such as "1h 30m" and "-2 days 4 hours". Accept one or more terms using parse's numeric syntax and case-insensitive unit spellings, but require an explicit unit for every term. Separate adjacent terms by one or more ASCII spaces; allow ASCII spaces between number and unit. A single leading minus applies to the whole sum; reject signs on later terms. Terms may occur in any order and repeat units. No leading/trailing whitespace, plus sign, punctuation separators or partial trailing garbage. Return NaN for malformed nonempty inputs; preserve parse's throw boundary for non-string, empty or >100-character input without requiring an exception subtype/message. Use the existing unit conversions including months/years. Do not broaden parse, parseStrict or ms parsing. Add public export/declarations, docs and regression tests.
